The package registers two HTTP routes for pages it renders in a web view: `POST
_native/api/events`, which builds whatever class the request names with
whatever arguments it carries, and `POST _native/api/call`, which calls
whatever bridge function it names. This application renders no web view, so
neither is used, and each is a door: the first is object injection by design,
and the second reaches every bridge function this plugin declares, the app
lock's and the secure store's included. Anything that ever got a page into a
web view here could walk through both. So the package registers neither.

